    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One engine this session expects to touch, qualified by the role it serves.</para>
<para>Replaces the four per-role engine fields <ref refid="struct_tryll_1_1_client_1_1_tryll_client_1_1_session_config" kindref="compound">SessionConfig</ref> carried through protocol v12. The server&apos;s catalog states each model&apos;s engine, so nothing here selects one — an entry only says &quot;expect to use this&quot;, which lets the server initialise that engine&apos;s backend at CreateSession instead of at first load.</para>
<para>The role is redundant for lookup and survives so a pre-warm log line reads (&quot;warmed llama-cpp for role language&quot;). It costs one byte on the wire. One role may name several engines, and naming none is normal. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
